			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 3360
			},
			"text": " What would be the cumulative energy of the hundreds of thousands of keystrokes required"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:03,360",
				"to": "00:00:04,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 3360,
				"to": 4360
			},
			"text": " to write a novel?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:04,360",
				"to": "00:00:07,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 4360,
				"to": 7720
			},
			"text": " There's a lot of engineering research into the force required to press keys, in part"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:07,720",
				"to": "00:00:10,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 7720,
				"to": 10680
			},
			"text": " because so many people suffer from repetitive strain injuries."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:10,680",
				"to": "00:00:13,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 10680,
				"to": 13880
			},
			"text": " Using data from a study of rubber dome keyboards, we can estimate that the energy required to"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:13,880",
				"to": "00:00:18,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 13880,
				"to": 18920
			},
			"text": " press a key is around 1.5 mJ for a letter key, and 2.5 for a big key like enter or space"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:18,920",
				"to": "00:00:19,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 18920,
				"to": 19920
			},
			"text": " bar."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:19,920",
				"to": "00:00:20,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 19920,
				"to": 20960
			},
			"text": " How much is 1.5 mJ?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:20,960",
				"to": "00:00:24,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 20960,
				"to": 24000
			},
			"text": " Well, it's enough to heat a drop of water by 1% of a degree."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:24,000",
				"to": "00:00:28,280"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 24000,
				"to": 28280
			},
			"text": " It's also enough to lift a squirrel 300 microns, all the way from the ground to the top of"
		},
